{
  "name": "ground-beetle",
  "_about": "The violet ground beetle (Carabus violaceus), 28 mm long: a narrow head with strong sickle jaws and long palps, thread antennae half its length; a heart-shaped pronotum and a waist behind it; long oval wing cases fused shut (it cannot fly), black and finely granular, a violet-purple rim round them and the pronotum; long slender black legs -- a night hunter of slugs and worms. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
